# ============================================================================
# FlowChemistry / Chapman-Jouguet detonation in 2 H2 + O2 + 7 Ar at 6.67 kPa, 298 K, STARTED FROM ITS ZND PROFILE
# (species.eos = pele, chem.backend = pele, species.order = 2; mechanism build, see input_0D_H2O2Ignition)
#
# This is the speed test of the detonation: the steady ZND solution (Cantera, same mechanism; table made by
#   bin/tests/venv_cantera/bin/python tests/FlowChemistry/reference/h2o2_check.py table --out <file> --length 0.3)
# is mapped onto the grid with the shock at x = 0.3 m (IC type profile1d) and must then travel at
# D_CJ = 1616.65 m/s with the von Neumann pressure 174.65 kPa at the front.  It is how unsteady detonation runs are
# started in the literature (e.g. Barwey, Ullman, Bielawski & Raman 2024, same mixture); a blast or piston start
# leaves this low-pressure mixture several per cent off D_CJ for more than a millisecond (input_1D_H2O2Detonation,
# changelog II.37).  1.2 m, 7680 cells = 0.156 mm = 9.7 cells per induction length, 530 microseconds.
# The table path is relative to bin/.  RESULT (2026-10-06): mean front speed 1615.8 m/s (-0.05 %), front pressure
# 174.8 kPa (+0.06 %), over 0.82 m of travel.
#
# Run (from bin/): mpirun -np 16 ./hydro2-2d-g++-bd ../tests/FlowChemistry/input_1D_H2O2Detonation_ZND plot_file=<dir>/output
# Check:           tests/venv_cantera/bin/python ../tests/FlowChemistry/reference/h2o2_check.py detonation <dir> --x0 0.3
